@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 12
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #344054
skinparam maxMessageSize 300
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #344054
  FontColor #101828
}
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #667085
  FontColor #101828
  BackgroundColor #F9FAFB
}
title Behavior - Delete a confirmed leaf item
actor "Authorized user" as actor
box "Frontend - Mission Control application" #E0F2FE
  participant "WorkItemDetailPage or WorkHierarchyPage / WorkItemDeleteDialog / WorkItemDeleteForm" as page
  participant "IWorkItemService / WorkItemService" as client
end box
box "Backend - MissionControl.Api" #D1FADF
  participant "CurrentAccountAuthorization" as access
  participant "WorkItemsController" as ctrl
end box
box "Backend - MissionControl.Application and Domain" #ECFDF3
  participant "ValidationBehavior" as validation
  participant "DeleteWorkItemCommandHandler" as handler
  participant "WorkItem" as entity
end box
box "Backend - MissionControl.Infrastructure" #FFF4E5
  database "Mission Control SQL" as db
end box
actor -> page : Choose Delete on a work item (the view's actionRequested with its WorkItemTarget)
page -> page : Open the confirmation naming the item from the WorkItemTarget, with nothing read on open; focus Cancel
alt Cancel or Escape
  actor -> page : Cancel
  page -> page : Close; send no request; focus returns to Delete
else Confirm
  actor -> page : Delete
  page -> page : Disable both buttons while pending (deleting state)
  page -> client : Build typed DeleteWorkItemCommand (workspace and item IDs; no version)
  client -> access : DELETE /api/workspaces/{id}/work-items/{itemId}
  access -> access : L2-002 validate signature, issuer, audience, subject, expiry
  access -> db : Read current status, role and credential version
  db --> access : Current account access
  alt Missing, invalid or expired JWT; deactivated account
    access --> client : 401; audit denial without payloads
    client --> page : sessionInterceptor calls SessionService.end(Unauthorized) once for this generation; the promise rejects with its 401 (nothing written); sign-in shows session-unsaved when a draft was dirty, then returns to the item
  else Account lacks work.delete (role changed to Collaborator while the dialog was open; profile P: work.delete is administrator-only)
    access --> client : 403; audit denial without payloads
    client --> page : sessionInterceptor calls SessionService.refreshCapabilities(); WorkItemDeleteForm sets forbidden: the dialog stays open with "Only administrators can delete work" in its alert, no reference ID, and Delete unavailable; focus moves to Cancel
    page -> page : The refreshed capabilities turn the layout's canDeleteWork false, so the page's Delete actions become unavailable with their written reason
  else Administrator (work.delete)
    access -> ctrl : Authorized request
    ctrl -> validation : Send DeleteWorkItemCommand through MediatR 12.5.0
    note right of ctrl : Both IDs are path IDs with a {id:guid} route constraint; a malformed ID matches no route and returns 404 before dispatch
    validation -> handler : Handle DeleteWorkItemCommand
    group Under the workspace lock
      handler -> db : BeginWorkspaceTransactionAsync takes the workspace lock first; LoadDeletionCheckAsync reads the item, child count, open sprint membership with its state, whether sprints are paused (Kanban), the parent, and the tracked sibling order, backlog order, and boards
      db --> handler : Current deletion conditions, or lock-wait timeout
      opt Item loaded
        handler -> entity : checkDeletion(childCount, openSprint, openSprintStatus, sprintsPaused)
        entity --> handler : The Domain DeletionBlocker naming every blocker found, or none
      end
      alt Workspace lock wait times out
        handler --> ctrl : 503 with Retry-After; nothing read or deleted
        ctrl --> client : ProblemDetails (unavailable)
        client --> page : Unavailable save, as for a 500: nothing deleted; alert with reference ID; focus stays on Try again, which resends only when chosen (failed state)
      else Workspace or item not found
        handler --> ctrl : 404; nothing changed
        ctrl --> client : ProblemDetails (not found)
        client --> page : WorkItemDeleteForm emits alreadyDeleted; the dialog closes with AlreadyDeleted; the page increments its refresh counter (the detail page opens the parent's detail first) and the toast says the item was already deleted, or, after the dialog relayed unconfirmed, the neutral info toast "'Publish team list for mentors' has been deleted."
      else DeletionBlocker returned: children, or a story in a planned or active sprint (L2-018.1, L2-018.2)
        handler --> ctrl : 409 DeletionBlocker naming every blocker found: child count; open sprint, its state, the story's status, and sprintsPaused; nothing changed
        ctrl --> client : ProblemDetails (blocked)
        client --> page : WorkItemDeleteForm puts each blocker's explanation in the dialog's alert region, which becomes its description; Delete gives way to Close, which receives focus; no retry
        alt Children only
          page --> actor : Move or delete the children first; Close only (has-children state)
        else Planned sprint while sprints are paused (Kanban, L2-027.3)
          page --> actor : Explains the pause: "Switch the project back to Scrum to change its plan, then delete the story."; Close (back to the opening page), plus Change delivery mode when canChangeMode (in-paused-sprint state)
          opt Change delivery mode
            actor -> page : Change delivery mode
            page -> page : Form emits changeModeRequested; the dialog closes with ChangeMode; the page calls inject(ProjectLayoutPage).openDialog(ChangeMode), which opens ModeChangeDialog
          end
        else Planned sprint
          page --> actor : "Change Sprint N's plan" (in-planned-sprint state)
          actor -> page : Change Sprint N's plan
          page -> page : Form emits changePlanRequested(sprintId); the dialog closes with ChangePlan(sprintId); the page navigates to /projects/:id/sprints/:sprintId/plan?remove={storyId}, which opens the plan with the story marked To remove
        else Active sprint, unfinished story
          page --> actor : "Remove from Sprint N" (in-sprint state)
          actor -> page : Remove from Sprint N
          page -> page : Form emits removeFromSprintRequested(sprintId); the dialog closes with RemoveFromSprint(sprintId); the page opens SprintScopeDialog in remove mode with removeStoryId and the target's scopeSummary; on SprintScopeOutcome Changed it increments its refresh counter and shows the "Scope updated" toast with the outcome's summary (TOAST_SERVICE), and on Outdated it increments the counter; while that dialog stays open, its forbidden output (an unexpected 403) shows the "Your access changed" toast without Retry
        else Active sprint, Done story
          page --> actor : Done stories stay with the sprint's outcomes; deletable once the sprint closes; any children named too; Close only (in-sprint-done state)
        end
      else Deletable leaf
        handler -> handler : L2-018 checkDeletion returned no blocker: a leaf outside open membership
        handler -> db : L2-039 / L2-040 RemoveWorkItem and AddAuditEvent, then SaveChangesAsync: delete item; remove its sibling position and, for a story, its StoryBacklogPosition and BoardPlacements as tracked children; compact and bump those orders; for a task increment the parent story's task revision only (the story's version and sprint versions unchanged); success audit
        note right of db : Closed SprintStoryOutcome rows have no cascading FK and stay unchanged (L2-018.4)
        alt Commit fails
          db --> handler : Roll back business state and success audit
          handler --> ctrl : Generic 500 with correlation ID
          ctrl --> client : Failure; no deletion claim
          client --> page : Nothing deleted; alert with reference ID; focus stays on Try again, which resends the same request only when chosen (failed state)
        else Commit succeeds
          db --> handler : Committed deletion
          handler --> ctrl : Deleted
          ctrl --> client : 204
          client --> page : WorkItemDeleteForm emits deleted; the dialog closes with Deleted
          page -> page : The outline increments its refresh counter, so its expanded branches and counts reread; the detail page opens the parent's detail, or the work outline for an initiative
          page --> actor : The "Task deleted" toast (named for the item's type) names the item; focus moves to the parent's row, or to the destination heading after navigation
        end
      end
    end
  end
end
opt No response to the deletion (timeout or network failure)
  client --> page : The deletion may have committed: the failed alert reads "We couldn't confirm whether the task was deleted" without a reference ID; WorkItemDeleteForm emits unconfirmed, which the dialog relays so the page rereads at once; Try again resends only when pressed, and a deletion that went through then returns 404 (AlreadyDeleted); because the dialog relayed unconfirmed, the page shows the neutral info toast "'Publish team list for mentors' has been deleted." instead of saying it was already deleted
end
note over ctrl, db
All rejection checks run under the lock before any write.
Unexpected failures return generic 500 plus correlation ID (L2-043).
Diagnostics exclude secrets and contact payloads.
end note
@enduml
